  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "f255edb8-9823-ed31-7748-e1f3daeb05a4",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "062b0a4b-5cca-51a9-a39d-0cf3f98720a3",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Yihan Lin, a cardiothoracic surgeon at Stanford University School of Medicine, along with her team, including Nicole Lin, a cardiothoracic resident, and Vongai Mlambo, a medical student, demonstrated their dedication by navigating logistical challenges to conduct workshops in Nairobi. Despite initial setbacks, the workshops proved to be highly beneficial, offering both novice and advanced learners the opportunity to enhance their suturing skills using simple materials and surgical instruments provided by the GlobalSurgBox. With overwhelming demand for such low-resource training, discussions are underway to expand the reach of GlobalSurgBox in Kenya. ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The team at CIME Nairobi extends their gratitude to Yihan, Nicole, and Vongai for their generosity and commitment to advancing surgical education.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
